is my recommendation  is that you put your own  oxygen mask on first before helping  others  metaphorically speaking and practically  speaking  all that means is unless you can take  care of yourself  you're not going to be able to take care  of your family and you're certainly not  going to be able to save anyone else  there are a million recommendations i  could give most of them are going to be  related to self-care  exercise diet etc i'm not going to  belabor those i'm going to give you two  perhaps  you haven't heard discussed quite as  much so the first is make plans  actually make plans what would you do  over the next 6 months  12 months consider traveling consider  doing all the things you would like to  do not because you can do them  but because there is value in the  planning it's going to force you to  think about  vaccines it's going to force you to  think about risks it's going to force  you to think about  logistics and this is to say  while your plans may end up worthless  there will still be tremendous value in  the planning  this is really important i think to  underscore and understand  that most plans do not survive first  contact with a customer with reality  with a punch in the face  but the active planning forces you to  ask questions and consider things  perhaps you wouldn't have come across  otherwise and there's a lot of value in  that so plan out the next 12 months  and consider different adventures  consider how you could make them work  and it's also going to be uplifting to  have something to even tentatively look  forward to  so i suggest doing this and the last is  control your information intake  i think over the last year it has become  a national and global sport to doom  scroll  that is to constantly look through  social media  and elsewhere at text from your friends  for all the worst things that have  happened today  anywhere in the world or especially  somewhere close to you  this is really unhelpful and  damaging in more respects than i can  even name  but suffice to say if it's not relevant  to your life if you're not going to  take action based on this new  information if it's not going to change  your behavior  if you can't affect some change if  you're not going to try to help  don't pay attention to it there's no  value  there is no value in unless we consider  the value to be  putting you in a terrible mood and  putting a dark lens over everything else  that you see that day  these technologies or at least the  content and the content providers are  very often incentivized  to make you as incensed or afraid or  angry as possible  i don't think that contributes to your  productivity or well-being so  really get your doom scrolling under  control consider deleting your social  media apps from your phone which is what  i have done  and i feel that that will provide  tremendous dividends and roi  in your life in a world with or without  covid  you
 

